        ("South Beach and the Art Deco district", "The National Register district runs from Sixth Street up to the Collins Canal and Dade Boulevard, between the ocean and Alton Road. It holds hundreds of hotels and apartment buildings put up between 1923 and 1943, so stucco, color and trim on a repair should match what is already there."),
        ("Star, Palm and Hibiscus Islands", "Three man-made islands finished in 1922 and reached from the MacArthur Causeway. Palm Island's entrance has a guard gate, so the crew needs to be on the visitor list before it pulls up. Hibiscus mixes mansions with converted apartments and condos."),
        ("The Venetian Islands", "Four belong to Miami Beach: San Marino, Di Lido, Rivo Alto and Belle Isle. Biscayne Island and San Marco are part of the City of [[city:miami|Miami]]. All sit along the Venetian Causeway, built in 1925 as a series of drawbridges, so a bridge opening can hold up the drive."),
